---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import { company, site, power, network, solar, compute } from '../data/site';

/* Calculated from the record, so the total can never drift from the parts. */
const totalSqft = site.buildings.reduce((n, b) => n + b.sqft, 0);
const tractAcres = site.tracts.reduce((n, t) => n + t.acres, 0);
---

<Content
  title={`${site.designation} — ${site.name} | ${company.full}`}
  description={`${site.acresRounded} in ${site.county}, Oklahoma, across three tracts. Buildings A, B and C total ${totalSqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft of existing building area; ${site.manufacturing.sqftTotal.toLocaleString()} sq ft of manufacturing is planned on Tract 1 and ${solar.tractAcres} acres are set aside for energy on Tract 3.`}
  kicker={`${site.designation} · ${site.county}, Oklahoma`}
  heading="One campus. Room to build."
  lede={`${site.address}. ${site.acresRounded} organised as manufacturing land, the existing buildings, and land for planned solar and storage. The three are at genuinely different stages, and this page keeps them apart.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Campus', value: `${tractAcres.toFixed(2)} acres`, note: 'Three tracts, owner-reported', count: true },
    { label: 'Existing buildings', value: `${totalSqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft`, note: 'A, B and C — gross, not white space', count: true },
    { label: 'Shared service', value: power.service, note: power.serviceScope, tone: 'gold' },
    { label: 'First compute', value: site.powerOn, note: 'Target, requires revalidation', tone: 'signal' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="today" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">On the ground</span></p>
    <h2 id="today">What exists, and what does not</h2>

    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>
          Three buildings stand on Tract 2 — A, B and C, {totalSqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft
          between them — behind a shared {power.service} distribution originating at
          Building C. That is the part that exists. None of the three has an established
          fit-out or commissioning status, and the gross floor area above is not certified
          white space or sellable rack area.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Tract 1 is empty land with {site.manufacturing.buildings} buildings planned on
          it. Tract 3 is empty land set aside for energy. Neither is under construction.
          What a tenant is underwriting is a fit-out inside buildings that exist, not a
          finished facility and not a greenfield promise.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="pull">
      <p>{tractAcres.toFixed(2)} acres, from three tract sizes.</p>
      <p>
        13.50 + 7.51 + 18.20. "Approximately 40 acres" is the rounded form of that sum
        rather than a second measurement, and the 0.79-acre difference is unexplained
        until the recorded survey settles it. We would rather show you the arithmetic than
        the round number on its own.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="land" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">The land</span></p>
    <h2 id="land">The parcel</h2>

    <div class="split">
      <dl class="spec">
        <div><dt>Address</dt><dd>{site.address}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>County</dt><dd>{site.county}, Oklahoma</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Acreage</dt><dd>{tractAcres.toFixed(2)} acres<span class="note">{site.acresNote}</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tenure</dt><dd>{site.ownership}<span class="note">{site.ownershipNote}</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Frontage</dt><dd>US-70<span class="note">Highway frontage at the address above — the parcel is reached directly from the state highway, not from a county section road.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Parcel ID</dt><dd><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: Bryan County assessor parcel number and legal description]</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Zoning</dt><dd><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: zoning classification and whether a data center is permitted by right]</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Utilities on parcel</dt><dd>Electrical service and fibre confirmed. <span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: water source, sanitary/septic, and natural gas availability]</span></dd></div>
      </dl>

      <figure class="photo">
        <div class="photo__frame">
          <svg class="photo__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="2.5" y="6" width="19" height="14" rx="2" />
            <circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3.5" />
            <path d="M8.5 6l1.4-2.2h4.2L15.5 6" />
            <path d="M3 3l18 18" />
          </svg>
          <p class="photo__state">Photograph not taken yet</p>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <b>[PHOTO NEEDED]</b> Aerial of the campus with the three tracts, Buildings A,
          B and C and the US-70 frontage visible, ideally flown in daylight with the
          boundary legible. A real photograph or an empty frame — and a render of the
          planned factory or solar field would be labelled as a concept, never shown as
          the site.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="tracts" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">The three tracts</span></p>
    <h2 id="tracts">One campus, organised in three parts</h2>

    <p>
      The tract schedule below is the record every other figure on this site is
      generated from. Two of the three tracts are undeveloped land with plans on them;
      only Tract 2 has anything standing.
    </p>

    <div class="scroller" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Tract schedule, scrollable">
      <table>
        <caption>Tract schedule, {site.designation}</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Tract</th>
            <th scope="col">Area</th>
            <th scope="col">Intended use</th>
            <th scope="col">State today</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {site.tracts.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{t.label}</th>
              <td class="num">{t.acres.toFixed(2)} acres</td>
              <td>{t.use}</td>
              <td>{t.state}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Total</th>
            <td class="num">{tractAcres.toFixed(2)} acres</td>
            <td>Sum of the three owner-reported tract sizes</td>
            <td>{site.acresNote}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-top: var(--s-7);">Planned manufacturing, Tract 1</h3>
    <p>
      {site.manufacturing.buildings} buildings of
      {' '}{site.manufacturing.sqftEach.toLocaleString()} sq ft each —
      {' '}{site.manufacturing.sqftTotal.toLocaleString()} sq ft in total — are planned for
      {' '}{site.manufacturing.scope.toLowerCase()}. Management targets a construction start
      {' '}{site.manufacturing.startTarget}. {site.manufacturing.startTargetNote} Nothing is
      under construction today, and this page will not say otherwise until work starts.
      {' '}<span class="todo">{site.manufacturing.allocation}</span>
    </p>

    <h3 style="margin-top: var(--s-6);">Three timelines, deliberately separate</h3>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Manufacturing</h3>
        <p>
          Two planned buildings on Tract 1; construction-start target
          {' '}{site.manufacturing.startTarget}, subject to confirmation of a dated
          schedule.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Data center</h3>
        <p>
          An {compute.gpus}-GPU initial deployment. Procurement, building assignment,
          fit-out, network acceptance and first paid workload are separate milestones —
          {' '}{site.powerOn} is an earlier target requiring revalidation, not a confirmed
          launch.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Energy</h3>
        <p>
          Survey and layout, a load and dispatch study, the utility process, funding,
          construction and commissioning. No completion date has been committed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="buildings" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">The buildings</span></p>
    <h2 id="buildings">Buildings A, B and C</h2>

    <p>
      Three existing buildings on Tract 2, of three different sizes, totalling
      {' '}{totalSqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft. This is gross existing building area — not
      certified white space, not sellable rack area, and not a commissioned data hall.
      Which building takes the first compute installation has not been confirmed. The
      house and office, {site.houseOffice.sqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft, are separately
      identified and excluded from these figures entirely.
    </p>

    <div class="scroller" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Building schedule, scrollable">
      <table>
        <caption>Building schedule, Site 01</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Building</th>
            <th scope="col">Footprint</th>
            <th scope="col">Role</th>
            <th scope="col">Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {site.buildings.map((b) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Building {b.id}</th>
              <td class="num">{b.sqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft</td>
              <td>{b.role}</td>
              <td>{site.buildingStatus}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Total</th>
            <td class="num">{totalSqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft</td>
            <td>Gross existing building area across {site.buildings.length} buildings</td>
            <td><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: clear height, slab loading, and roof structure per building]</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">House / office</th>
            <td class="num">{site.houseOffice.sqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft</td>
            <td>{site.houseOffice.note}</td>
            <td>Separate {power.houseOfficeService} supply</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top: var(--s-5);">
      Structural and mechanical detail a tenant will ask for before signing —
      clear height, floor loading in lbs/sq ft, door and equipment access,
      and the route for liquid cooling pipework — is
      {' '}<span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: as-built drawings and structural report for Buildings 1–3]</span>.
      We would rather show you nothing than a number we have not measured.
    </p>

    <figure class="photo" style="margin-top: var(--s-6);">
      <div class="photo__frame">
        <svg class="photo__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="2.5" y="6" width="19" height="14" rx="2" />
          <circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3.5" />
          <path d="M8.5 6l1.4-2.2h4.2L15.5 6" />
          <path d="M3 3l18 18" />
        </svg>
        <p class="photo__state">Photograph not taken yet</p>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <b>[PHOTO NEEDED]</b> Ground-level exterior of Building 1 and, separately, the
        empty interior of Building 1 before fit-out. The empty interior is the more
        persuasive image: it is the thing a tenant is buying.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="why" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">05</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Location</span></p>
    <h2 id="why">Why Mead</h2>

    <p>
      The location argument is not about a metro or a fibre hub. It is about what was
      already sitting on this parcel when we bought it.
    </p>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The service was already there</h3>
        <p>
          {power.service}, shared across Buildings A, B and C from Building C. A
          greenfield build starts by asking a utility for load; this starts with
          distribution already installed. What it can carry as IT load is a separate
          question, and it follows an engineering review.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The buildings were already there</h3>
        <p>
          {totalSqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft of existing building across A, B and C
          removes ground-up construction from the critical path. The first deployment is a
          fit-out rather than a build — and a fit-out that has not started.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The land is owned, not optioned</h3>
        <p>
          {site.ownership} in {site.county}. Which entity holds it, and what liens sit
          against it, is being documented before this page says more than that.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Connectivity is planned</h3>
        <p>
          {network.publicCopy} Rural Oklahoma is often written off on connectivity; this
          parcel looks better than that, and a quote, an order and a live circuit are
          three different stages.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="diligence" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">06</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Diligence</span></p>
    <h2 id="diligence">What we have not published yet</h2>

    <p>
      Anything below is a real diligence item a tenant or lender will ask for. We have
      not published a number because we do not yet have one we would stand behind. This
      list is here so you can ask for the ones that matter to you rather than discover
      the gap in week six.
    </p>

    <ul class="bullets">
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: ALTA survey and title commitment]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: FEMA flood zone determination for the parcel]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: Phase I environmental site assessment]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: geotechnical report — bearing capacity for equipment pads and the solar array]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: seismic and wind design criteria used for Buildings 1–3]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: water availability and volume, and whether any cooling loop needs it]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: Bryan County and Oklahoma tax treatment applicable to the site]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: nearest commercial airport and drive time for hands-on site visits]</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="next" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">07</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Next</span></p>
    <h2 id="next">The electrical position is the reason this site is worth reading about</h2>
    <p>
      {tractAcres.toFixed(2)} acres is a good starting position. What makes the schedule
      worth examining is that distribution is already installed and three buildings are
      already standing — so the question becomes what they can carry, which is a question
      an engineer can answer rather than a queue.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/power">Read the power story</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact">Arrange a site visit</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Content>
